From: pocket-debs
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: h264: Wait for the second field before outputting a pair
Description:
 A field pair is decoded with two requests that share one capture
 buffer: the first field is queued with V4L2_BUF_FLAG_M2M_HOLD_CAPTURE_BUF
 and the second field uses a sub-request. The picture handed to
 output_picture() is the first field, and only its own request was
 waited for. When the request of the second field was still pending,
 which happens for the last pair at the end of the stream (drain), the
 capture buffer was pushed downstream while the driver was still writing
 the second field into it, and the lines of that field came out wrong
 from time to time.
 .
 Let the first field track the last request of the second field when
 that one is queued, as the picture already tracks its last sub-request
 in slice mode. output_picture() then waits for it; the pending requests
 are completed in queue order, so this also completes the request of the
 first field, and the capture buffer is dequeued with the last one. The
 second field cannot be looked up at output time, the first field does
 not hold a reference on it.
Forwarded: no
License: LGPL-2.0-or-later (as the patched file)
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
---
diff --git a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech264dec.c b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech264dec.c
index 6d7f09a..cfdb543 100644
--- a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech264dec.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech264dec.c
@@ -1327,6 +1327,14 @@ gst_v4l2_codec_h264_dec_submit_bitstream (GstV4l2CodecH264Dec * self,
     goto done;
   }
 
+  /* The first field of a pair is the picture that gets output and holds the
+   * capture buffer, which is complete only once the last request of the
+   * second field is done: let the first field track that request. */
+  if (picture->second_field && picture->other_field)
+    gst_h264_picture_set_user_data (picture->other_field,
+        gst_v4l2_request_ref (request),
+        (GDestroyNotify) gst_v4l2_request_unref);
+
   gst_h264_picture_set_user_data (picture, g_steal_pointer (&request),
       (GDestroyNotify) gst_v4l2_request_unref);
   ret = TRUE;
